sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Even when slowly growing multiway systems show early apparent randomness in their state counts, they typically end up showing some form of repetition (sometimes with long periods, such as 1071 steps).";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Slowly growing multiway systems eventually become repetitive";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Multiway Systems” (from p. 204), p. 207. Scope: slowly growing multiway systems"
}
